%% seq_01b_testing_auth_context_bridge.mmd
%% Updated 2026-07-10 (verified).
%% Reader intent: Understand dev/test-only auth support surfaces that bridge seeded user identity, token pair issuance, refreshed org context, and web session bootstrap.
%% Key boundary: Test/support auth only; production OAuth redirect/callback lives in seq_01_auth.mmd.
%% Current caveat: These routes mount only in development|test and use api-ops-internal transport. They are tooling support, not production contract.
%% Runtime source:
%%   - POST /api/testing/token-login
%%   - POST /api/testing/token-refresh
%%   - POST /api/testing/session/bootstrap

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor T as Tester / Dev
    participant C as Test Client
    participant R as Auth Test Routes
    participant U as ensureTestingUser
    participant O as ensureTestingUserOrganization
    participant TS as SessionTokenService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant S as Web Session

    Note over T, S: ISSUE ORG-AWARE TOKEN PAIR
    T->>C: POST /api/testing/token-login
    C->>R: email, provider?, organizationId?, systemRole?
    R->>U: create/find seeded user
    U->>DB: upsert user + oauth provider if needed
    R->>O: ensure approved org membership / current org
    O->>DB: find or create workspace membership
    O-->>R: org-aware identity ready
    R->>TS: issueForUser(user, organizationId)
    TS-->>R: accessToken + refreshToken
    R-->>C: token pair JSON

    Note over T, S: ROTATE ACTIVE ORGANIZATION
    T->>C: POST /api/testing/token-refresh
    C->>R: refreshToken + organizationId?
    R->>TS: refresh(refreshToken, requestedOrganizationId)
    TS-->>R: refreshed token pair
    R-->>C: token pair JSON

    Note over T, S: BRIDGE BEARER TOKEN INTO WEB SESSION
    T->>C: POST /api/testing/session/bootstrap
    C->>R: Authorization: Bearer accessToken
    R->>TS: verifyAccessToken(accessToken)
    TS-->>R: verified user + org context
    R->>DB: persist user.current_organization_id if present
    R->>S: session.put(current_organization_id)
    R->>S: auth.use('web').login(user)
    R-->>C: authenticated session + org-aware response
